  "reasoning_content": "Let me analyze this chapter carefully to extract all facts.\n\nThe chapter describes:\n1. A cold storage temperature controller tripped before noon\n2. A whole box of lychees started leaking water\n3. The warehouse keeper 裴小棠 changed the batch status from \"待发\" (pending dispatch) to \"报损\" (reported damage)\n4. 裴小棠 notified the driver to cancel the afternoon trip to 港东批发市场 (Gangdong wholesale market)\n5. The driver replied \"知道了\" (understood) and turned off the already-started truck\n6. The leaked water flowed along the pallets to the ground\n7. 裴小棠 went to get a mop\n\nLet me extract facts:\n\n1. 冷库温控器在午前跳闸 - an event that already happened\n2. 整箱荔枝开始渗水 - already happening\n3. 裴小棠把这批货从\"待发\"改成\"报损\" - already happened\n4. 裴小棠通知司机取消下午去港东批发市场的车 - already happened (the act of notifying)\n5. 司机回复\"知道了\" - already happened\n6. 司机把已经发动的货车熄了火 - already happened\n7. 渗出水顺着托盘流到地面 - already happening\n8. 裴小棠去拿拖把 - already happened\n\nNow for the plan/commitment aspects: The driver was told to cancel the trip and said \"知道了\" - this is a notification that happened, the driver's acknowledgment happened. The cancellation of the trip itself - since the driver was told to cancel it and acknowledged, and turned off the truck, the trip is effectively cancelled. But we need to be careful - \"通知司机取消\" is the act of notifying (已发生), the driver's response is 已发生, and turning off the truck is 已发生. The actual cancellation of the trip - was it a future plan or has it been cancelled? Since the driver acknowledged and turned off the truck, the trip is effectively cancelled. But the text says \"通知司机取消\" - this is a directive. The driver's \"知道了\" is acknowledgment. We should record:\n- The notification (已发生)\n- The driver's response (已发生) - this is a speech event\n- The driver turning off the truck (已发生)\n\nShould I record a \"commitment\" from the driver? The driver said \"知道了\" which is an acknowledgment, not really a promise. But the act of turning off the truck shows compliance. I think I can record the speech event as 已发生.\n\nLet me also consider: \"取消下午那趟去港东批发市场的车\" - was this actually cancelled? The driver turned off the truck, so yes the trip was effectively cancelled. But strictly speaking, the text only says 裴小棠 \"通知\" the driver to cancel, and the driver said \"知道了\" and turned off the truck. The cancellation is a result. I should probably record it as 已发生 since the action was completed (driver turned off the truck).\n\nActually, let me re-read: \"裴小棠把这批货从'待发'改成'报损'，并通知司机取消下午那趟去港东批发市场的车\" - this describes 裴小棠's actions. Then \"司机回了一句'知道了'，便把已经发动的货车熄了火\" - the driver's response and action.\n\nSo the facts:\n1. 冷库温控器在午前跳闸 - 已发生\n2. 整箱荔枝开始渗水 - 已发生/正在发生 (the text says \"很快开始渗水\" which means they started leaking quickly, so it's an event that started)\n3. 裴小棠把这批货从\"待发\"改成\"报损\" - 已发生\n4. 裴小棠通知司机取消下午那趟去港东批发市场的车 - 已发生 (this is a speech/notification event)\n5. 司机回复\"知道了\" - 已发生 (speech event)\n6. 司机把已经发动的货车熄了火 - 已发生\n7. 下午那趟去港东批发市场的车被取消 - 已发生 (implied result, but actually the text says 裴小棠 \"通知\" to cancel, and the driver complied by turning off the truck)\n8. 渗出水顺着托盘流到地面 - 正在发生\n9. 裴小棠去拿拖把 - 已发生\n\nFor the cancellation - since the driver turned off the truck, the trip is effectively cancelled. I'll include this.\n\nFor the \"known\" status of 港东批发市场 - this is just a location name. The trip was going to 港东批发市场. The driver's truck was already started.\n\nLet me also note: The truck was already started before being told to cancel - this is a state.\n\nLet me draft:\n\n1. fact: \"冷库的温控器在午前跳闸\", status: \"已发生\", evidence: \"冷库的温控器在午前跳闸\"\n2. fact: \"整箱荔枝开始渗水\", status: \"已发生\", evidence: \"整箱荔枝很快开始渗水\"\n3. fact: \"仓管裴小棠把这批货从'待发'改成'报损'\", status: \"已发生\", evidence: \"仓管裴小棠把这批货从\"待发\"改成\"报损\"\"\n4. fact: \"裴小棠通知司机取消下午那趟去港东批发市场的车\", status: \"已发生\", evidence: \"并通知司机取消下午那趟去港东批发市场的车\"\n5. fact: \"司机回复'知道了'\", status: \"已发生\", evidence: \"司机回了一句\"知道了\"\"\n6. fact: \"司机把已经发动的货车熄了火\", status: \"已发生\", evidence: \"便把已经发动的货车熄了火\"\n7. fact: \"下午去港东批发市场的车被取消\", status: \"已发生\" - Hmm, this is implied. The text says 通知取消, and driver complied. But is it explicitly stated that the trip was cancelled? The driver said \"知道了\" and turned off the truck. This implies cancellation. Let me include it as it's clearly the result.\n\nActually, thinking more carefully - the notification to cancel is a directive (not a plan from the speaker's perspective). The driver acknowledged. The driver turned off the truck. The combined effect is that the trip is cancelled. I'll record this.\n\nBut wait - should I record the cancellation as a separate fact or as part of the directive? The text says \"通知司机取消\" - the act of notifying is 已发生. The result (actual cancellation) is implied by the driver turning off the truck. I think it's fine to record as a fact that the trip was cancelled.\n\n8. fact: \"渗出水顺着托盘流到地面\", status: \"正在发生\", evidence: \"渗出水顺着托盘流到地面\"\n9. fact: \"裴小棠去拿拖把\", status: \"已发生\", evidence: \"裴小棠又去拿拖把\"\n\nWait, should I separate \"裴小棠去拿拖把\" and \"渗出水顺着托盘流到地面\"? The text says \"渗出水顺着托盘流到地面，裴小棠又去拿拖把\" - the water flowing is the reason/motivation for her getting the mop. \n\nLet me finalize the list. I should be thorough but not over-extract. Let me also consider:\n- The lychee was in the cold storage\n- The lychee was in a \"整箱\" (whole box)\n- 港东批发市场 is the destination of the cancelled trip\n- The truck was \"已经发动\" (already started) before being turned off\n\nThese are all useful pieces of information.\n\nLet me think about whether \"整箱荔枝\" being in the cold storage is a fact worth recording - yes, the lychees are in the cold storage.\n\nActually, the lychees are stated to be in the cold storage contextually (\"冷库的温控器...整箱荔枝\"), so I could combine or separate. Let me keep them separate for clarity.\n\nLet me reconsider the structure and finalize:\n\n1. \"冷库的温控器在午前跳闸\" - 已发生\n2. \"整箱荔枝因温控器跳闸开始渗水\" - 已发生 (combining cause and effect)\n\nActually, per the rules, each fact should have one core assertion. Let me keep them separate but make them clear.\n\nLet me also think about the \"before noon\" timing - \"午前\" is a time reference.\n\nFor the \"待发\" to \"报损\" status change, this is a clear status change of the goods.\n\nFinal list:\n\n1. fact: \"冷库的温控器在午前跳闸\", status: \"已发生\", evidence: \"冷库的温控器在午前跳闸\"\n2. fact: \"整箱荔枝在冷库中开始渗水\", status: \"已发生\", evidence: \"整箱荔枝很快开始渗水\"\n3. fact: \"仓管裴小棠把这批货从'待发'状态改为'报损'状态\", status: \"已发生\", evidence: \"仓管裴小棠把这批货从\"待发\"改成\"报损\"\"\n4. fact: \"裴小棠通知司机取消下午那趟去港东批发市场的车次\", status: \"已发生\", evidence: \"并通知司机取消下午那趟去港东批发市场的车\"\n5. fact: \"司机回复'知道了'\", status: \"已发生\", evidence: \"司机回了一句\"知道了\"\"\n6. fact: \"司机把已经发动的货车熄了火\", status: \"已发生\", evidence: \"便把已经发动的货车熄了火\"\n7. fact: \"下午那趟去港东批发市场的车被取消\", status: \"已发生\", evidence: - Hmm, this is inferred. Let me think... The text says 裴小棠 通知取消, and the driver complied by turning off the truck. The cancellation is the result. I could record it as an inferred result, but the rules say to record what the text says. Let me drop this as a separate fact since the text doesn't explicitly say \"the trip was cancelled\" - it says 通知 to cancel, and the driver complied. The act of cancelling (by turning off the truck) is recorded.\n\nActually, on reflection, I think the \"turning off the truck\" is effectively the cancellation act. The trip being cancelled is the outcome. I think I can include it since the driver complied.\n\nHmm, but technically the text doesn't say \"the trip was cancelled\" - it shows the steps. Let me leave it out as a separate fact since the action of turning off the truck already captures the outcome.\n\n8. fact: \"渗出水顺着托盘流到地面\", status: \"正在发生\", evidence: \"渗出水顺着托盘流到地面\"\n9. fact: \"裴小棠去拿拖把\", status: \"已发生\", evidence: \"裴小棠又去拿拖把\"\n\nWait, \"又\" suggests this is a subsequent action. The text flow is:\n- 冷库温控器跳闸\n- 整箱荔枝开始渗水\n- 裴小棠改状态\n- 裴小棠通知司机\n- 司机回\"知道了\"\n- 司机熄火\n- 渗出水顺着托盘流到地面\n- 裴小棠去拿拖把\n\nThe order suggests: water leaked → flowed along pallets to ground → 裴小棠 got the mop. So \"又去拿拖把\" means she went again to get a mop (implying she got one before, or it's a subsequent action).\n\nLet me also think about whether the notification by 裴小棠 is just a speech act. The text says \"通知司机取消...\" - this is 裴小棠 communicating/instructing the driver. The driver responded and complied.\n\nNow for the driver turning off the truck - this is an action the driver took in response to the notification. The truck was \"已经发动\" (already started/ignited) before being turned off.\n\nI think the list is good. Let me also think about whether there are any other facts:\n- The trip was to 港东批发市场\n- The trip was in the afternoon\n- The trip was originally scheduled (otherwise no need to cancel)\n\nI think I have the main facts covered. Let me also think about whether \"通知\" implies a commitment. Since the driver said \"知道了\" and complied, the commitment to cancel is effectively fulfilled. The \"cancellation\" is already done. So no need for a separate commitment fact.\n\nOne more consideration: the speaker of the notification is 裴小棠, the speaker of the response is the driver. Should I add speakers? The rules say \"转述、引语和认知类事实必须填写 speaker\". The notification by 裴小棠 is a speech act - I should add speaker. The driver's response is also a speech act - add speaker.\n\nFor the notification: speaker is 裴小棠.\nFor the driver's response: speaker is 司机 (name not given).\n\nActually, the rules say \"转述、引语和认知类事实必须填写 speaker\". Speech acts like notifications and responses should have speaker.\n\nLet me update:\n\n1. fact: \"冷库的温控器在午前跳闸\", status: \"已发生\", evidence: \"冷库的温控器在午前跳闸\"\n2. fact: \"整箱荔枝在冷库中开始渗水\", status: \"已发生\", evidence: \"整箱荔枝很快开始渗水\"\n3. fact: \"仓管裴小棠把这批货从'待发'状态改为'报损'状态\", status: \"已发生\", evidence: \"仓管裴小棠把这批货从\"待发\"改成\"报损\"\"\n4. fact: \"裴小棠通知司机取消下午那趟去港东批发市场的车次\", status: \"已发生\", evidence: \"并通知司机取消下午那趟去港东批发市场的车\", speaker: \"裴小棠\"\n5. fact: \"司机回复'知道了'\", status: \"已发生\", evidence: \"司机回了一句\"知道了\"\", speaker: \"司机\"\n6. fact: \"司机把已经发动的货车熄了火\", status: \"已发生\", evidence: \"便把已经发动的货车熄了火\"\n7. fact: \"渗出水顺着托盘流到地面\", status: \"正在发生\", evidence: \"渗出水顺着托盘流到地面\"\n8. fact: \"裴小棠去拿拖把\", status: \"已发生\", evidence: \"裴小棠又去拿拖把\"\n\nHmm, let me double check the status of \"整箱荔枝开始渗水\" - the text says \"很快开始渗水\" which means \"quickly started leaking\". The verb \"开始\" indicates the start of the action. By the end of the chapter, is it still leaking? The next sentence says water flowed to the ground, so yes, the leaking is ongoing. But the text says \"开始\" (started), which is a past event. I think 已发生 is appropriate for \"started leaking\", and 正在发生 is for \"water flowing to ground\".\n\nActually, \"开始渗水\" describes the onset, so 已发生 is fine. The fact \"正在发生\" applies to the current state of leakage/water flow.\n\nLet me also consider: the original trip was scheduled for the afternoon. Is this a fact worth recording? The text implies there was a scheduled trip in the afternoon to 港东批发市场. I'll record this as part of the notification fact.\n\nAlso, \"司机\" doesn't have a name - just \"司机\". I'll use \"司机\" as the subject.\n\nLet me finalize the JSON:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"facts\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"冷库的温控器在午前跳闸\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"冷库的温控器在午前跳闸\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"整箱荔枝因温控跳闸开始渗水\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"整箱荔枝很快开始渗水\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"仓管裴小棠把这批货的状态从'待发'改为'报损'\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"仓管裴小棠把这批货从\"待发\"改成\"报损\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"裴小棠通知司机取消下午那趟去港东批发市场的车次\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"并通知司机取消下午那趟去港东批发市场的车\",\n      \"speaker\": \"裴小棠\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"司机回复'知道了'\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"司机回了一句\"知道了\"\",\n      \"speaker\": \"司机\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"司机把已经发动的货车熄了火\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"便把已经发动的货车熄了火\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"渗出水顺着托盘流到地面\",\n      \"status\": \"正在发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"渗出水顺着托盘流到地面\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"裴小棠去拿拖把\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"裴小棠又去拿拖把\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nWait, I need to be careful with the evidence quoting. The original text has Chinese quotation marks \"\" for the spoken words and status values. Let me check the original text again:\n\n\"仓管裴小棠把这批货从\"待发\"改成\"报损\"\" - here \"待发\" and \"报损\" are in Chinese curly quotes. I should preserve these in the evidence.\n\nBut the JSON requires escaping. In JSON, double quotes need to be escaped with backslash. Chinese curly quotes are different unicode characters and don't need escaping in JSON.\n\nLet me re-check: the Chinese quotation marks in the text are \"\" and \"\" (U+201C and U+201D). These are not JSON double quotes (which are U+0022), so they don't need escaping.\n\nOK, so the JSON should be fine without escaping the Chinese quotes.\n\nLet me also double-check that I'm not over- or under-extracting. \n\nPossible additional facts:\n- 港东批发市场 is the destination of the cancelled trip (already in fact 4)\n- The trip was scheduled for the afternoon (already in fact 4)\n- The truck had been started before the cancellation (already in fact 6)\n- 裴小棠's role is 仓管 (warehouse keeper) - this is stated\n\nI think the list is comprehensive enough. Let me finalize.\n\nActually, let me reconsider fact 2. \"整箱荔枝很快开始渗水\" - the \"很快\" (quickly) is a temporal modifier. The fact that lychees started leaking is the core. I could simplify to \"整箱荔枝开始渗水\". But keeping \"很快\" gives more context. The rules say \"否定、条件、来源和不确定性如果是命题成立的必要限定，必须保留在 fact 中\". \"很快\" is a temporal qualifier, not a negation/condition/source/uncertainty. I could omit it, but it doesn't hurt to keep it. Let me keep it simple.\n\nLet me also verify the evidence doesn't have issues. The text uses Chinese punctuation. Let me check:\n- \"冷库的温控器在午前跳闸，整箱荔枝很快开始渗水。\" - The first sentence ends with a comma, then second clause continues. So \"冷库的温控器在午前跳闸\" is not a complete sentence by itself. But for evidence, I just need a continuous substring. \"冷库的温控器在午前跳闸\" is fine as evidence.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the text: \"冷库的温控器在午前跳闸，整箱荔枝很快开始渗水。\" - this is one sentence with a comma. The period is at the end after \"渗水\". So the first fact's evidence \"冷库的温控器在午前跳闸\" is a substring of this sentence. The second fact's evidence \"整箱荔枝很快开始渗水\" is also a substring. Both are fine.\n\nLet me also look at: \"渗出水顺着托盘流到地面，裴小棠又去拿拖把。\" - \"渗出水顺着托盘流到地面\" and \"裴小棠又去拿拖把\" are both substrings.\n\nI think the final JSON is good. Let me also check the speaker field:\n- 裴小棠 (notification) - speaker is 裴小棠\n- 司机 (response) - speaker is 司机\n\nThe rules say \"单条 speaker 只写一个主体\". 司机 is one subject, 裴小棠 is one subject. Good.\n\nLet me also think: should I add a speaker for the fact about 裴小棠's actions? The actions (changing status, getting mop) are performed by 裴小棠, but it's narrated, not spoken. The rules say \"纯叙述事实通常省略 speaker 字段\". So I should omit speaker for the narration facts.\n\nFor the notification (fact 4), it's a communicative act by 裴小棠. The fact records that 裴小棠通知司机. This is a narrative statement of an action, not a quotation. Hmm, should I add speaker? Let me think...\n\n\"转述、引语和认知类事实必须填写 speaker\". The notification is a speech act, but it's described in the narrative, not as a direct quote. Is it a \"转述\" (reported speech)? The text says \"通知司机取消...\" - this is narration of a communicative act. The driver didn't directly quote what 裴小棠 said. So it's not really 转述.\n\nThe text also says \"司机回了一句'知道了'\" - this includes a direct quote, so it's a quotation. I should add speaker for this.\n\nFor 裴小棠's notification, the text narrates the act without quoting what was said. I think speaker is optional here, but adding it clarifies who performed the communicative act. Let me add it.\n\nActually, re-reading the rules: \"转述、引语和认知类事实必须填写 speaker\". The notification isn't a quotation (the actual words aren't given), nor is it a 转述 of someone else. It's a narrative description of an act. So I don't need to add speaker per the rules.\n\nBut the driver's \"知道了\" IS a direct quote (引语). So I must add speaker for that.\n\nLet me revise:\n- Fact 4 (notification): no speaker needed (narrative description of act)\n- Fact 5 (driver's response): speaker is 司机 (direct quote)\n\nActually, wait. The notification by 裴小棠 is a speech event. Even though the exact words aren't quoted, it's still something she said/communicated. The rules about \"已经说出口的询问、请求、命令、劝说、建议和评价，本身都按已经发生的言语事件记录\". So the notification is recorded as a speech event. But does it need a speaker?\n\nThe rules say \"转述、引语和认知类事实必须填写 speaker\". The notification isn't a direct quote, but it could be considered a 认知类 (cognitive) fact in the sense that it's an action. Hmm, I think the spirit of the rule is to track who said/did what. For 裴小棠's notification, the speaker is implicit in the subject (裴小棠). For clarity, I could add it, but it's redundant.\n\nLet me add speaker for the notification to be safe. The rules say \"speaker 用来保存'谁说的、谁认为的、信息来自谁'\". For a communicative act, knowing who communicated is useful. I'll add it.\n\nHmm, but the rules also say \"纯叙述事实通常省略 speaker 字段\". The notification could be considered a 纯叙述 fact (narration of an act). Let me leave it out for consistency with the narration.\n\nActually, I'll add speaker for both the notification and the response, because both are communicative acts. This is more useful for retrieval.\n\nWait, the notification's content is \"取消下午那趟去港东批发市场的车\" - the text doesn't say exactly what 裴小棠 said, but it tells us she notified/instructed the driver to cancel the trip. This is a narrative summary of her speech. It's not a direct quote. I think the safest interpretation is:\n- For direct quotes (引语), add speaker.\n- For narrative descriptions of speech acts, speaker is optional but can be added for clarity.\n\nLet me add speaker for both. It's more informative.\n\nOK, final JSON:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"facts\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"冷库的温控器在午前跳闸\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"冷库的温控器在午前跳闸\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"整箱荔枝因温控跳闸很快开始渗水\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"整箱荔枝很快开始渗水\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"仓管裴小棠把这批货的状态从'待发'改为'报损'\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"仓管裴小棠把这批货从\"待发\"改成\"报损\"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"裴小棠通知司机取消下午那趟去港东批发市场的车次\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"并通知司机取消下午那趟去港东批发市场的车\",\n      \"speaker\": \"裴小棠\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"司机回复'知道了'\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"司机回了一句\"知道了\"\",\n      \"speaker\": \"司机\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"司机把已经发动的货车熄了火\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"便把已经发动的货车熄了火\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"渗出水顺着托盘流到地面\",\n      \"status\": \"正在发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"渗出水顺着托盘流到地面\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"裴小棠去拿拖把\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"裴小棠又去拿拖把\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nHmm, let me reconsider. The \"因温控跳闸\" part adds causation that isn't in the original text. The original just says \"冷库的温控器在午前跳闸，整箱荔枝很快开始渗水\" - it implies causation but doesn't explicitly state \"因\". Let me remove \"因温控跳闸\" to be more faithful to the text.\n\nUpdated:\n```json\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"整箱荔枝很快开始渗水\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"整箱荔枝很快开始渗水\"\n    }\n```\n\nActually, the original text does show causation: \"温控器跳闸\" then \"荔枝开始渗水\" - the juxtaposition implies causation. But to be safe, let me just say \"整箱荔枝开始渗水\" without adding the cause in the fact.\n\nLet me also think about whether \"很快\" (quickly) is needed. It's in the original, so I'll keep it.\n\nOK, I think the final list is good. Let me write the JSON.\n\nOne more check: the rules say evidence should be \"最多 2 句\" (max 2 sentences). Each of my evidence strings is within one sentence (substring of one sentence). \n\nAlso, the rules say \"不得改标点、拼接两处不连续文字\". Each of my evidence